meta {
  name: Get Assessment Start Info
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/assessments/start?application_id={{applicationId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  application_id: {{applicationId}}
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Assessment Room screen. No slot id in the URL — a slot is just a timing
  wrapper around a template, the student never picks one directly.
  `application_id` (required) is resolved server-side:
  Application.admissionCycle.assessmentTemplateId -> the template's
  currently active slot. One attempt covers the whole Application (every
  course listed on it), not a single course — application_id, not
  application_course_id.

  409 ConflictError "This application is not currently at the assessment
  stage" if Application.formStatus isn't "submitted".
  409 ConflictError "Assessment not required for this application" if the
  admission cycle's assessment_required is false.
  409 ConflictError "No assessment configured for this admission cycle" if
  the admission cycle has no assessment_template_id set (college-admin
  configures both of these on the Application Form / Admission Cycle
  itself, not per course).

  `slot` in the response is `null` if the resolved template currently has
  no active slot scheduled — render a "not currently scheduled" state on
  the Room screen, not an error, in that case.

  Returns the template's section breakdown, instructions (heading +
  description + an optional client-defined icon key), `total_marks`, and
  `total_duration_secs` — both computed as sums over the currently-approved
  normal paper's questions (both 0 if no normal paper is approved yet).
  `has_active_trial_paper` tells the client whether to show/enable "Take
  Trial of Assessment". `is_within_window`/`has_window_passed` are both
  `false` when `slot` is null. `my_attempt` (`{id, status}` or `null`) is
  always resolved now, so the Room screen can render "Resume Assessment"
  instead of "Start Assessment" for a returning student.
}
